cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "contribution-kit: Reusable toolkit for attributing a modeled quantity to its contributing factors"
abstract: >-
  Declarative error attribution for prediction pipelines. Failure regimes are
  Boolean conditions over CSV columns, tested with risk and odds ratios;
  crossed regimes form a factorial table whose cells are ranked by
  attributable burden against an analyst-chosen baseline; and an exact
  Shapley decomposition of the prediction formula screens its inputs, with
  jointly determined inputs grouped into one player.
